S580 LRC n=14 certificate calculus

FORMAL OBJECTS
SpeedRow := (n, S, time-site labels, owner labels, quotient labels).
CertificateSection := witness_1_over_n | cheap_pair | positive_measure | ledger_failure | residual.
Gate := a partial rule SpeedRow -> CertificateSection or NamedResidual, with restriction maps between rows.
Vitali handoff := the divisibility wall n|v, where THM-398 moves from construction to measure.
Cascade product := ordered product of conditional clearances supplied by gates G0..G10.
Target theorem form := every row exits through a witness/positive_measure section, or every terminal residual SCC is impossible.

GATES
name | status | output | residual
G0_no_multiple_n_clock | PROVED | closed witness t=1/n | none
G1_Cprime_reduction | PROVED reduction | LRC(n) follows from Cprime | Cprime itself: n|v implies M(S)>1/n
G2_dominance_or_long_interval_dodge | PROVED partial Cprime | positive measure | all-short Vitali alignment for a small multiple
G3_all_short_Cprime_residual | OPEN | positive measure for small multiples | one AP of thin arcs is arc-aligned enough to cover a fixed open safe set
G4_paired_or_anchored_cheap_pair | REDUCTION plus verified split | unblocked small-pair pinch witness | block-all rows must be proved positive measure
G5_fixed_boundary_owner_functor | BOUNDED scaffold | 64 fixed fibres with speed-owner labels | unbounded realization independence
G6_unit_lift_cheap_sieve | BOUNDED zero residual | cheap pair fires before exchange | simultaneous multi-unit no-cheap rows
G7_apex_lift_certificate_sheaf | BOUNDED zero restriction residual | global cheap section or positive-measure restriction | unbounded apex monodromy over fixed fibres
G8_endpoint_cover_circuit_positivity | OPEN bridge | positive measure from failed gluing | cover circuits with no private pivot/owner
G9_tie_wall_limit_functor | OPEN formalization | boundary perturbations become a labelled tie-wall object | AP/Vstar perturbation-direction ambiguity
G10_certificate_calculus_closure | PROPOSED | every row has a section or a named positive-measure residual | terminal residual acyclicity

NAMED RESIDUALS
- Cprime itself: n|v implies M(S)>1/n: G1_Cprime_reduction
- all-short Vitali alignment for a small multiple: G2_dominance_or_long_interval_dodge
- one AP of thin arcs is arc-aligned enough to cover a fixed open safe set: G3_all_short_Cprime_residual
- block-all rows must be proved positive measure: G4_paired_or_anchored_cheap_pair
- unbounded realization independence: G5_fixed_boundary_owner_functor
- simultaneous multi-unit no-cheap rows: G6_unit_lift_cheap_sieve
- unbounded apex monodromy over fixed fibres: G7_apex_lift_certificate_sheaf
- cover circuits with no private pivot/owner: G8_endpoint_cover_circuit_positivity
- AP/Vstar perturbation-direction ambiguity: G9_tie_wall_limit_functor
- terminal residual acyclicity: G10_certificate_calculus_closure

